        "original_id": "be62b2ac-3fd0-54ac-9fb8-ba7d9027ffe2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: V. K. Krishna Menon, Jawaharlal Nehru, Satya Narayan Gourisaria\n- Organizations: India League\n- Roles: Prime Minister of India, diplomat, politician, company secretary, Gandhian\n- Topics: Indian nationalism, Indian independence movement, Indian politics\n\nFacts:\n- Jawaharlal Nehru was born on 14 November 1889 and later became the first Prime Minister of India and a central figure in Indian politics before and after Indian independence.\n- V. K. Krishna Menon was born on 3 May 1896 and was an Indian nationalist, diplomat, and politician.\n- V. K. Krishna Menon founded the India League as an Indian independence movement organization.\n- V. K. Krishna Menon was described by some as the second most powerful man in India after his ally Jawaharlal Nehru.\n- Satya Narayan Gourisaria is an Indian-born British company secretary, Gandhian, and former secretary of the India League.\n- Jawaharlal Nehru died on 27 May 1964.\n- V. K. Krishna Menon died on 6 October 1974.",
